  "text": "That vulnerability is actually one of your greatest strengths here. Mental health isn't about being an expert with all the answers; it's about showing up, being honest, and saying, \"This is what I'm navigating right now.\"\n\nWhen you share your raw, unfiltered experiences, you're not just talking *at* people—you're creating a bridge for them to realize they aren't alone. Often, the very thing that scares us (our own pain or confusion) is exactly what others need to hear most. You don't have to be perfect or fully healed to make a difference; you just have to be real.\n\nHow does it feel when you imagine someone reading your first post? Do you see it as a conversation starter rather than a lecture?",
